     <p>That wardrobe is the step most runs miss. Double taps are rare this early, and a single press on the door gives no sign that the gesture wants repeating. Order matters as well: the panel only becomes a swipe target once the unit itself has been tapped, and the clothes inside cannot travel to the man until the door is open. Skip the panel and the sequence stops there, with the wardrobe still shut and the man still sitting in the tub. One role reversal, one appliance that wants two gestures, and one container that wants a double press: that is where a run loses the thread.</p>
