+    <p>The ghost absorbs six of the sixteen moves: the towel at 1, the nurse's coat at 2, the bandage at 4, the notebook and pen at 5, the hammer at 8 and the pump at 11 all end on the same patient. That builds a habit (find an object, drag it to the ghost), which the level breaks at steps 6, 7 and 9. The candy goes to the child at step 6, the cosmetics to the girl at step 7, the scissors to the boy at step 9. Four patients share one waiting room, and the ghost is only the largest of them.</p>
     <p>Two cards carry more than one thing. Step 5 is the notebook and the pen together, so a single drag has two objects in it, and step 12 is a click on the photo in the ghost's hand rather than on the ghost. The target there is the size of a card, not the size of a figure. Step 3 is the only swipe: the axe hangs above the ghost's head and has to be pushed up out of the way. Fourteen of the sixteen moves are drags, one is that click, one is that swipe, which makes the odd gesture the easiest thing in the clinic to get wrong.</p>
